<%#
  Calls surface.

  There is no call history list yet - PlConnectCallItem records only start to
  exist once a call has actually happened, and browsing them is a separate
  piece of work. What already works here: starting a new direct (1:1) call
  without first navigating into an existing conversation. Picking a person
  from the shared user picker (mode "call") resolves/creates the 1:1 chat via
  /pl_connect_api/open_direct and navigates to it with a start_call query
  param; PlConnectWorkspaceController#chat_element validates that param and
  pl_connect_call_controller.js starts the call as soon as the chat has
  finished loading (see its pendingValue). Group/channel/team calls are
  started from inside the conversation itself instead (same call/video
  buttons in the message pane header, see PlConnect::CallService) - this
  surface only ever resolves a single person.
%>
<div class="flex min-h-0 w-full items-center justify-center bg-base-200 p-6">
  <div class="flex max-w-md flex-col items-center gap-4 text-center">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-video text-5xl text-base-content/20" aria-hidden="true"></i>

    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">
      <%= I18n.t("pl_connect.call.start_new_call_title") %>
    </h2>

    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/60">
      <%= I18n.t("pl_connect.call.start_new_call_text") %>
    </p>

    <div class="flex gap-2">
      <button type="button"
              class="btn btn-outline btn-sm"
              data-action="pl-connect-user-picker#open"
              data-pl-connect-picker-mode="call"
              data-pl-connect-picker-start-call="audio">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-phone" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <%= I18n.t("pl_connect.call.start_audio_call") %>
      </button>
      <button type="button"
              class="btn btn-primary btn-sm"
              data-action="pl-connect-user-picker#open"
              data-pl-connect-picker-mode="call"
              data-pl-connect-picker-start-call="video">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-video" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <%= I18n.t("pl_connect.call.start_video_call") %>
      </button>
    </div>

    <%#
      Stated up front so nobody plans around a capacity that does not exist:
      a peer-to-peer mesh stays usable up to roughly four participants. Larger
      conferences would need a media server (SFU), which is out of scope.
    %>
    <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50">
      <%= I18n.t("pl_connect.call.mesh_limit_hint", count: PlConnect::CallService.mesh_participant_limit) %>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
